Subject: [PATCH] src/lab-process-mail: Add a loop to run under daemon(8)
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: orkosmpvsuxnxxqnytoovmxszwxtywnp
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:25:31 +0000

lab-process-mail drains the inbox once and exits, so new mail waits
until the operator switches terminals and runs it again by hand.
lab-process-mail-loop reruns it on an interval, so a supervisor can
keep the inbox answered without anyone watching.

It is a separate program rather than a flag so the drain logic stays
a single pass that is easy to test, and it stays in the foreground so
daemon(8), or s6, owns detaching, logging, and the pidfile.

A failed run stops the loop instead of retrying. A stuck message stays
oldest in the inbox, so a retry would spend an agent pass on it every
interval while the stuck notice has already gone out.
